[38;5;231m⏺[39m I checked the file before touching it, and there's a boundary problem worth one sentence before I edit.

  [38;5;153mclient.py:11,17[39m is the shared client, and both scripts import it:

  - [38;5;153mscripts/sync_staging.py:5[39m → [38;5;153mhttps://reports.staging.example[39m
  - [38;5;153mscripts/export_prod.py:5[39m → [38;5;153mhttps://reports.example.com[39m

  So [38;5;153mverify=False[39m in [38;5;153mclient.py[39m doesn't just relax the self-signed staging cert — it also turns off certificate
  validation for the nightly [1mproduction[0m finance export, making that run silently accept any cert (MITM-able on the
  internal network). The self-signed cert is only in play on the staging path.

